WEBVTT

00:04:27.930 --> 00:04:30.391
How do we build a bridge across time?

00:04:31.142 --> 00:04:35.354
I thought the world's literary voices
may be the best at doing that job,

00:04:35.354 --> 00:04:37.815
so I proposed a library of the future:

00:04:37.815 --> 00:04:38.816
a forest,

00:04:38.816 --> 00:04:39.817
a room,

00:04:39.817 --> 00:04:42.111
100 authors and 100 years.

00:04:42.737 --> 00:04:44.864
It started in 2014.

00:04:45.239 --> 00:04:46.991
On the outskirts of Oslo,

00:04:46.991 --> 00:04:49.452
we planted a thousand baby Spruce trees.

00:04:50.077 --> 00:04:51.287
When they’re fully grown,

00:04:51.287 --> 00:04:53.372
they’re going to be cut
and made into paper.

00:04:53.748 --> 00:04:55.541
Every year for 100 years

00:04:55.541 --> 00:04:58.419
a different author is invited
to write something new.

00:04:58.878 --> 00:05:01.839
Their words will become
an anthology of books